{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "reseact_box",
    "description": "ReSEACT 0-D box model, stage 2: SuperFast gas chemistry (mounted BY REF, using the new reaction_systems ref import) + FastJX photolysis (by ref) + NEI2016 surface emissions (by ref), with dry/wet deposition. A Clock model advances FastJX's solar time with the integrator: FastJX's cos_sza uses the t_utc parameter (not the independent variable t), so on its own the j-rates are frozen; param_to_var drives FastJX.t_utc from Clock.t_now = t_utc0 + t, giving a real diurnal photolysis cycle over a multi-hour run. Met (T, P) and site (lat, lon) are prescribed parameters (a single well-mixed box).\n\nEmissions: NEI2016MonthlyEmis is a pure-I/O data-loader consumer — its 69 NEI2016.<SP> fields have NO defining equation and are injected at the RHS boundary through the provider seam, so `simulate` must be given a provider per field (see box_run.jl, which reads the real EPA 12US1 NetCDF at the box's grid cell). NEI's own t_ref and the Clock's t_utc0 are set to the SAME instant at runtime so the emission diurnal/day-of-week scaling and the solar zenith angle refer to one absolute clock."
  },
  "reaction_systems": {
    "SuperFast": { "ref": "../../../EarthSciModels/components/gaschem/superfast.esm" }
  },
  "models": {
    "FastJX": { "ref": "../../../EarthSciModels/components/gaschem/fastjx/fastjx_interp_troposphere.esm" },
    "Solar": { "ref": "../../../EarthSciModels/lib/solar.esm" },
    "Clock": {
      "variables": {
        "t_utc0": { "type": "parameter", "units": "s", "default": 1462345200.0, "description": "Sim start time (Unix s); solar time = t_utc0 + t." },
        "t_now":  { "type": "observed",  "units": "s", "description": "Current UTC time advancing with the integrator.",
                    "expression": { "op": "+", "args": ["t_utc0", "t"] } }
      },
      "equations": []
    },
    "SuperFastDepositionSink": { "ref": "../../../EarthSciModels/components/atmospheric_deposition/superfast_deposition_sink.esm" },
    "NEI2016Emis": { "ref": "../../../EarthSciModels/components/earthsci_data/nei2016_monthly.esm" }
  },
  "coupling": [
    { "type": "coupling_import", "ref": "../../../EarthSciModels/couplings/fastjx_superfast.esm",
      "bind": { "Photolysis": "FastJX", "Chem": "SuperFast" } },
    { "type": "coupling_import", "ref": "../../../EarthSciModels/couplings/nei2016_superfast.esm",
      "bind": { "Emissions": "NEI2016Emis", "Chem": "SuperFast" } },
    { "type": "variable_map", "from": "Clock.t_now", "to": "Solar.t_utc", "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "Advance the solar clock with the integrator." },
    { "type": "variable_map", "from": "Solar.cos_zenith", "to": "FastJX.cos_sza", "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "Drive the photolysis rates from the solar zenith angle. fastjx_interp_troposphere takes cos_sza as an input (it carries no solar geometry of its own) and interpolates the 18-band TROPOSPHERIC actinic flux on (cos_sza, P) — unlike fastjx.esm, whose F_i are top-of-atmosphere flux x cos_sza, which overstates j_O31D by ~200x and collapses the ozone.\n\nNOTE (open EarthSciAST issue, not worked around here): cos_sza sits upstream of all 18 F_i bands and every j-rate sums all 18, and the tree-walk re-evaluates an observed at each reference site instead of caching it — so the Solar chain, which reaches cos_zenith through datetime.* (the boxed, allocating path), is walked ~250x per RHS call: ~3,260 datetime evaluations, 313 KB and 930 us per call. That makes the 24 h stiff solve very slow. The fix belongs in the tree-walk (cache observeds in topological order), not in this model." },
    { "type": "operator_compose", "systems": ["SuperFast", "SuperFastDepositionSink"],
      "description": "Merge the D(SuperFast.<X>) ~ -(k_dry+k_wet)*X deposition sink onto the chemistry ODEs. Dep-rate params k_* set at runtime (box: prescribed vdep/H)." }
  ]
}
